Description: Hyprland desktop shell built on Quickshell
 FormalShell is a single-process desktop shell for Hyprland: bar,
 launcher, notifications, lock screen, panels and screensaver, themed
 from the wallpaper with matugen.

Package: formalshell-eds
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Evolution Data Server calendar companion CLI for FormalShell
 Reads calendar events from Evolution Data Server over D-Bus and prints
 them as JSON for FormalShell's calendar.

Package: formalshell-ttfx
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Provides: ttfx (= 0.4.0)
Conflicts: ttfx
Replaces: ttfx
Description: terminal text effects as a single static binary
 ttfx renders animated terminal text effects. FormalShell's screensaver
 parses its ANSI frame stream.

Package: formalshell-tensaku
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, wl-clipboard
Provides: tensaku (= 0.26.6)
Conflicts: tensaku
Replaces: tensaku
Description: screenshot annotation for Wayland
 Tensaku, a fork of Satty, annotates a screenshot with arrows, text,
 markers, highlights and blur in a GTK 4 window.

Package: formalshell-matugen
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Provides: matugen (= 4.1.0)
Conflicts: matugen
Replaces: matugen
Description: Material You colour generation from a wallpaper
 matugen derives a Material colour scheme from an image and renders it
 through user templates. FormalShell themes itself and GTK and Qt with it.

Package: formalshell-nerd-fonts-symbols
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: Nerd Fonts symbols-only font
 The Symbols Nerd Font from Nerd Fonts, with no text glyphs. FormalShell
 takes the launcher's distro marks and its nerd icon set from it.

Package: formalshell-clipssh
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, openssh-client, wl-clipboard
Provides: clipssh
Conflicts: clipssh
Replaces: clipssh
Description: paste local clipboard images into terminal tools over SSH
 clipssh uploads the image on the local Wayland clipboard to a remote host
 and copies the uploaded file's path to the clipboard.

Package: formalshell-localsend-cli
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Built-Using: ${misc:Built-Using}
Description: headless LocalSend v2 client
 Peer scan, file send and unattended receive over the LocalSend v2
 protocol, without the GUI app.

Package: formalshell-iphone-bridge
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 gir1.2-glib-2.0,
 libglib2.0-bin,
 python3,
 python3-gi,
Description: JSONL bridges over ancs4linux ANCS and AMS D-Bus signals
 omarchy-iphone-bridge and omarchy-iphone-ams turn ancs4linux's
 notification and media D-Bus signals into JSON lines for FormalShell.

Package: formalshell-ancs4linux
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
 bluez,
 python3-dasbus,
 python3-gi,
 python3-typer,
Provides: ancs4linux
Conflicts: ancs4linux
Replaces: ancs4linux
Description: ANCS and AMS bridge exposing an iPhone as system D-Bus services
 ancs4linux pairs with an iPhone over Bluetooth LE and republishes its
 notifications and now playing state on the system bus.
